# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js App Router project following the latest official documentation from Vercel.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (v2.0.0)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the dependency tree

### 2. Code Integration
Modified `/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next"`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag (after ThemeProvider)

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide for Next.js App Router (v13.5+):
- Used the framework-specific import from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
- Placed the component in the root layout file to track all pages
- Positioned at the end of the body tag to avoid interfering with existing components

## Framework Detection
- Framework: Next.js 14.2.5 (App Router)
- Package Manager: npm
- Project Structure: App directory-based routing

## Verification
- ✓ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- ✓ No TypeScript errors
- ✓ All static pages generated successfully
- ✓ Dependencies installed and lock file updated
- ✓ Code follows existing project structure and patterns

## Next Steps
To enable Speed Insights tracking in production:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard for this project
3. Metrics will start appearing after users visit the deployed site

## Notes
- The SpeedInsights component is a zero-config component that automatically tracks Core Web Vitals
- It only runs on Vercel deployments (no impact on local development)
- The implementation preserves all existing functionality and styling
